            "18. Explain the significance of discipline and manners in public places, with reference to the course material.",
            "Discipline in public places is necessary because shared environments work only when people consider one another’s needs.\nRoads, hospitals, public transport, parks and educational institutions depend on cooperation and respect for common rules.\nBehaviour such as queue-jumping, littering, loud disturbances or careless use of facilities may seem minor, but it imposes costs on others and can create serious inconvenience.\nGood manners express an awareness that public space belongs to everyone, not to the loudest or most powerful person.\nDiscipline also involves self-control: people must follow rules even when no one is watching and accept responsibility when they make mistakes.\nThe course’s discussions of manners encourage readers to distinguish genuine civic conduct from mere outward politeness.\nA respectful person speaks courteously but also acts fairly, keeps shared spaces clean and protects the dignity of others.\nSchools, families and public institutions can model these habits, while individuals practise them daily.\nPublic discipline is therefore a foundation of civic responsibility and a more considerate society."
