            "8. Explain about bioremediation. [15 marks]",
            "Answer: • Definition: use of microorganisms, plants or their enzymes to remove, degrade or detoxify environmental pollutants.\n• In situ: treatment at the contaminated site; examples include bioventing, biosparging and natural attenuation.\n• Ex situ: contaminated soil/water is removed and treated elsewhere; examples include landfarming, composting, biopiles and slurry bioreactors.\n• Mechanism: microbes use or transform pollutants as substrates or convert them into less harmful products.\n• Factors: oxygen, nutrients, moisture, pH, temperature, pollutant bioavailability and microbial population.\n• Advantages: may be cost-effective and cause less disturbance.\n• Limitations: slow, site-specific and ineffective for some persistent or toxic pollutants; monitoring is required."
